From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: openEuler RISC-V Package Automation <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] build: leave ISA selection to the distribution

The release build hard-codes -march=native. Under the RISC-V QEMU build
route GCC interprets the host-native selection as an invalid RISC-V ISA
string. Distribution compiler flags already carry the target ISA, so remove
the conflicting override.

Patch-Source: openEuler RISC-V package CI failure analysis
Patch-License: MIT
Upstream-Status: Not Submitted (automated upstream writes are not authorized)
---
 src/CMakeLists.txt | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/CMakeLists.txt b/src/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/src/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -41,7 +41,6 @@ target_compile_options(
   bongocat_options
   INTERFACE
     $<$<CONFIG:Release>:
-    -march=native
     -fomit-frame-pointer
     -funroll-loops
     -finline-functions
-- 
